> from the stairs.  There are no monsters left on that level, and
> anything I kill lower down is not fresh by the time I can get to the
> altar.  There's a neutral altar at DL 5 with still a decent number of
> monsters around, but I don't know if I dare try to convert it while my
> god is upset at me (and has probably lowered my luck, too).
> 
> What are my options for getting back on my god's good side?

You need to offer something big and by big I mean corpses of tough 
monsters. The easiest IMHO is giant mimic.

Try to live without your god's graces and just work downwards. You might 
stumble on chaotic altar deep enough that tough enough monsters are 
generated. You shouldn't try to convert altars before you have done your 
quest because it might convert you instead.

If you find a wish you can use later, you can go to the chaotic altar 
and wish for tough enough corpses to sacrifice. Ask for two dragon 
corpses of such colour that you are lacking an intrinsic. If you get 
both you can sacrifice the other and eat the other.

If you find a wish you have to use immediately, you can wish for two 
cursed scrolls of genocide. Go back to the chaotic altar and read the 
cursed scroll of genocide and ask for giant mimics. These are easy to 
kill and will be tough enough to mollify your chaotic god.

